-The harness then knows it can terminate the loop.
+The high-level loop above stops when there are no tool calls; that is a different stopping convention. With `finish`, the harness must recognize the call, return `final_answer`, and stop rather than send it back for another model turn. The function's return value alone does not stop the loop.
 
